            <li>— Limited Murrieta-area concrete contractors participate in LSAs</li>
            <li>— Google doesn't assess Murrieta soil knowledge or HOA experience</li>
            <li>— Available contractors change based on who's currently running ads</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">
        <span class="font-bold text-gray-800">Best for:</span> Homeowners who want a credential-verified starting point and prefer calling directly over submitting a form.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Option 4 -->
    <div class="border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-7 mb-8">
      <div class="flex items-start gap-4 mb-4">
        <span class="bg-gray-200 text-gray-700 font-bold text-lg rounded-full w-10 h-10 flex items-center justify-center shrink-0">4</span>
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-800">Nextdoor</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-500 text-sm mt-1">Neighborhood recommendations for high-stakes decisions</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
        For a high-dollar concrete project, Nextdoor is especially valuable because you can see which contractors have recently poured driveways or patios in your specific Murrieta neighborhood — and you can contact those neighbors to ask how the work held up over time. Concrete cracking issues often don't appear for 1–3 years; a neighbor who had work done two years ago is a better reference than a fresh online review.
      </p>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-4">
        <div>
          <h4 class="font-bold text-gray-800 mb-2">Pros</h4>
          <ul class="text-sm text-gray-600 space-y-1">
            <li>✓ Can see work that's been done in your specific neighborhood and soil conditions</li>
            <li>✓ Can ask neighbors about durability over time — not just first impressions</li>
